<title>RUSSIA: Russian Q1 oil production, refining slip yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Russian Q1 oil production, refining slip yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-04-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russian oil output in the first quarter of 1997 slipped 0.5 percent from year-ago levels to 72.6 million tonnes (5.81 million barrels per day), the State Statistics Committee said on Monday.</p>
<p>Russia refined 43.4 million tonnes (3.47 million bpd) of oil in January-March, two percent lower than year-ago levels, it said. The committee gave the following data --</p>
<p>RUSSIAN Q1 1997 OIL PRODUCTION (MILLION TONNES)</p>
<p>				 Q1 1997	  as pct of</p>
<p>						     Q1 1996</p>
<p>Oil				72.6		99.5</p>
<p>Refined oil		    43.4		98.0</p>
<p> gasoline			 6.5		99.0</p>
<p> diesel			  11.4		99.0</p>
<p> heavy fuel oil		16.7		99.5</p>
<p> lubricants		     0.5		79.0</p>
<p>Natural gas</p>
<p> (billion cubic metres)   156.0		98.0</p>
<p>Gas condensate		  2.2		99.6</p>
<p>-- Moscow Newsroom +7095 941 8520</p>
